  "failure_mode": "OCR emits glyphs and symbol runs for plotted marker ink. Existing mask-review policy correctly withholds their masks, allowing real markers to survive, but retains duplicate semantic text evidence at the same locations.",
  "responsible_subsystem": "ProductionAutomaticDetectionAdapter after marker acceptance, before calibration, semantic reasoning and Review projection.",
  "hypothesis": "Interpret an already flagged, unmasked, unreviewed Original Annotation/Other glyph as marker evidence when an accepted non-Other marker at the unchanged classifier operating point has its center inside the actual OCR polygon and its bounding square overlaps at least half of the OCR bounding area. Preserve all reviewed, masked, tick, heading, legend, participant and axis-title readings. Preserve marker geometry, classification and existing inference batches.",
  "isolated_change": "Filter the corroborated duplicate glyph from downstream semantic OCR, bind the derived result cache to original OCR and explicit marker associations, append a provenance warning, and retain the original reading, alternatives and geometry as rejected OCR audit evidence in the Review projection. No text replacement, invented values, new model or recognizer run.",
  "rejected_initial_shadow": "The first min-area overlap rule admitted small false marker proposals inside misread Probe words on train images. It is rejected. Coverage now uses the OCR region area. The first CSV aggregate also included other-split predictions; the corrected shadow selects only predictions from the evaluated split. No runtime implementation or inference was run for either shadow.",
